BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Livewhale": "https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/21256-the-rediscovery-of-george-nash-walker-the-price-of"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_livewhale
SUMMARY:The Rediscovery of George "Nash" Walker: The Price of Stardom in J
 im Crow America
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T153000
DTSTAMP:20260701T144850Z
UID:20260910T190000Z-21256@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T120000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,328,328/627_cs_-_The_Rediscovery_of_George_Nash_Walk
 er.rev.1782942306.jpg
CATEGORIES:Department Events,District Events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lecture on George "Nash" Walker by Dr. Daniel At
 kinson.  The lecture will focus on the first biography of George Walker\, 
 a uniquely Afro-American tale of innovation and triumph despite the odds\;
  the story of an underdog with a bite!The Rediscovery of George "Nash" Wal
 ker is the first biography dedicated to the life and cultural contribution
 s of George Walker\, an actor\, writer\, and producer who revolutionized B
 lack American theatre in the early twentieth century. Drawing on archival 
 resources\, newspaper accounts\, memoirs\, oral histories\, and writings b
 y Walker himself\, Daniel E. Atkinson traces Walker's rise from a medicine
  show performer to a leading figure in American popular culture.  Dr. Atki
 nson is an independent scholar and the Assistant Director of the August Wi
 lson estate. He earned his doctorate in ethnomusicology from the Universit
 y of Washington\, where he specialized in Afro-American music and culture.
   This lecture is funded by a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior College Fou
 ndation Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowment.Click here to join t
 he lecture through Zoom. (https://santarosa-edu.zoom.us/j/9741460790)&#160
 \;  &#160\;Click here for Dr. Atkinson's Instagram profile. (https://www.i
 nstagram.com/jazzworkerbee/)&#160\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20260701T214850Z
LOCATION:Doyle Library\, Room 4520 - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/21256-the-rediscovery-of-george-n
 ash-walker-the-price-of
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join us for a lecture on George "Nash" W
 alker by Dr. Daniel Atkinson.</p><p>  The lecture will focus on the first 
 biography of George Walker\, a uniquely Afro-American tale of innovation a
 nd triumph despite the odds\; the story of an underdog with a bite!</p><p>
 <em>The Rediscovery of George "Nash" Walker</em> is the first biography de
 dicated to the life and cultural contributions of George Walker\, an actor
 \, writer\, and producer who revolutionized Black American theatre in the 
 early twentieth century. Drawing on archival resources\, newspaper account
 s\, memoirs\, oral histories\, and writings by Walker himself\, Daniel E. 
 Atkinson traces Walker's rise from a medicine show performer to a leading 
 figure in American popular culture.</p><p>  Dr. Atkinson is an independent
  scholar and the Assistant Director of the August Wilson estate. He earned
  his doctorate in ethnomusicology from the University of Washington\, wher
 e he specialized in Afro-American music and culture.</p><p>  This lecture 
 is funded by a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior College Foundation Randolp
 h Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowment.</p><p><a href="https://santarosa-e
 du.zoom.us/j/9741460790" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Click here to join
  the lecture through Zoom.</a>&#160\;</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p><a href="https
 ://www.instagram.com/jazzworkerbee/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Click 
 here for Dr. Atkinson's Instagram profile.</a>&#160\;</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:21256
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80
 /height/80/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,328\,328/627_cs_-_The_Rediscovery_of_Ge
 orge_Nash_Walker.rev.1782942306.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/Los_Angeles
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
END:VEVENT
